From ed17cd07457c27e0b8731ef7222e1069b01b7fc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chaoso85 <216391968+chaoso85@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:45:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: octagon: sdhc2 no-1-8-v (fixed 2.95 V
 vqmmc)

Found by: SSH dmesg from the running rescue: the SD card is set up as
"UHS-I speed DDR50", then every ~60 s "mmc2: Timeout waiting for hardware
interrupt" (Cmd 0x063a = CMD6, ADMA Err 3) and ios falls back to
3.3 V high-speed.

What was wrong before: vqmmc-supply is l13a_2p95, a fixed ~2.95 V rail
that cannot switch to 1.8 V, yet sdhci advertised UHS-I, so the
card was put into DDR50 and the periodic retune failed. no-1-8-v keeps
the slot at 3.3 V high-speed. (No reference project used; found on the
phone.)

Signed-off-by: chaoso85 <216391968+chaoso85@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon.dtsi
index f4ebd7bc032..5735d4f8d21 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon.dtsi
@@ -1172,6 +1172,10 @@ &sdhc2 {
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vreg_l13a_2p95>;
 
 	cd-gpios = <&pm8994_gpios 8 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+
+	/* vqmmc (l13a) is fixed 2.95 V: UHS-I 1.8 V signalling cannot work; the card negotiated DDR50 and then
+	 * timed out on the periodic retune CMD6 (SDHCI timeout every ~60 s). Stay at 3.3 V high-speed. */
+	no-1-8-v;
 };
 
 &adsp_pil {
-- 
2.43.0

